      <h2 id="does-collagen-help">Does collagen help stretch marks?</h2>
      <p>There is no evidence that it does, because nobody has tested it. Searching the published literature for an oral collagen supplement with stretch marks as an endpoint returns nothing: not a positive trial, not a negative one. A dermatology review of the question put it bluntly, saying there are zero clinical trials testing whether collagen supplements prevent or treat stretch marks.</p>
      <p>That is a different statement from "collagen does not work". It means the question has never been asked properly, and anyone answering it confidently is reasoning from something else. The most widely copied figure on the internet claims collagen with vitamin C cuts stretch mark risk by 20 to 40% in pregnancy. Following that number back leads to a single page that says it summarises peer-reviewed research, names no study, and sells collagen. We could not find a primary source for it. Treat it as marketing.</p>

